 ] Add a test/AC exercising a mutation command (e.g. session B `rebar transition <id>` or `rebar comment`) on a ticket held by A that asserts the `WARN:` naming A is emitted BEFORE the mutation applies (read-precedes-write).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: 'a `transition <id> in_progress closed` run by another session warns about holder A and *then* clears the provenance — the read precedes the write'","Testing steps only run `rebar show <id>` and `rebar comment <id>`; no transition/mutation-ordering assertion","AC list has no criterion covering a mutation command emitting WARN before applying the mutation"],"finding":"The Approach makes a specific ordering claim — that a `transition <id> in_progress closed` run by another session 'warns about holder A and *then* clears the provenance — the read precedes the write' — but no acceptance criterion or test step exercises a mutation command's warn-before-mutate ordering; all tests use `show`/`comment` (non-mutating reads).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbb5aced8790f6cc8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (read-precedes-write paragraph) / Testing / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n29f7372f53616b8a","priority":0.625,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A regression that computes the warning AFTER the mutation applies (holder cleared) would emit no WARN for `transition`/`reopen`, yet all listed tests stay green because they never mutate a held ticket"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a test: claim as A, then as B run a mutating single-ticket command and assert stderr contains `WARN:` + holder `A` while the mutation still succeeds — proving the warning is read from pre-mutation state.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_re